{"event_type":"review","id":"c2a2a9d0afb04d4c9fc1416da49c5e5d8e47fbb127873c822021e138fcd67d33","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T21:51:59Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cc5bacb3feacd7fa77e8add03cf9636cb86337860f4e4fe8eec05c0081d69f75","sha256":"cc5bacb3feacd7fa77e8add03cf9636cb86337860f4e4fe8eec05c0081d69f75"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9e19c73a1696fce2689eeac80111c87194c13f0d5df12b25feb16995c8aecead","sha256":"9e19c73a1696fce2689eeac80111c87194c13f0d5df12b25feb16995c8aecead"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d067a27af7d34650b362b5baf2b7f632e1f8bd6094c0d728d4dad1809ddaae5e","sha256":"d067a27af7d34650b362b5baf2b7f632e1f8bd6094c0d728d4dad1809ddaae5e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e42d5faf2acf15809207e0f1a93b285a71537bd3d97885b43a1a6830e37e9cd0","sha256":"e42d5faf2acf15809207e0f1a93b285a71537bd3d97885b43a1a6830e37e9cd0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a59ad7b60925ffe66b976d9a262c646372a8eb861dab7dacaf5c60779092bb13","sha256":"a59ad7b60925ffe66b976d9a262c646372a8eb861dab7dacaf5c60779092bb13"}],"attempt_id":"f8ad084d4746ab5235f9958d439cd2fda3c9e8dccb759b8762b989e5efc36584:0:1","base":"48e1175c28f40ffbd6e43ea2149f47c5181c7c66","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"c70f1d1d782d1cdc35da51087d59ac3b3faf5877","body":"**Preserve Python float spelling in generated `raw` values.**\n\nAt `src/policy/crq/jsonValue.ts`, Line 148, `pythonNumberText(1)` returns `\"1\"`. Python float text requires `\"1.0\"`; exponent formatting also differs, such as `\"1e-07\"`. ([raw.githubusercontent.com](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.12.0/Objects/floatobject.c))\n\nConsequently, `parseJsonValue(JsonNumber.float(1).raw)` returns an integer, not a float. Use Python-compatible formatting for the default `raw` value.\n\nBased on learnings, defer this P2/Minor finding to a follow-up issue.","id":"f55e9ccbf3243993388c69a94addf237f9a8333d8b2ba42d0e9d38b4e8966fc8","intervals":[[148,148]],"path":"src/policy/crq/jsonValue.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve Python float spelling in generated `raw` values."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"e7038b722b4ae03e235594943a0a4cfa054b3ba2","body":"**Preserve case-insensitive `strptime` literals.**\n\nAt `src/policy/crq/utc.ts:99`, `parseIso('2026-11-15t12:00:00Z')` throws. Python 3.14.10 accepts this input because `strptime` compiles its format with `IGNORECASE`. Add the `i` flag to preserve that acceptance contract. ([raw.githubusercontent.com](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.14.10/Lib/_strptime.py))\n\nBased on learnings, defer this minor compatibility fix to a follow-up issue.","id":"149aeb712e055bee7d32e41ce2e8c25e164de6b5264ebaaf3cf45d58fd840906","intervals":[[99,99]],"path":"src/policy/crq/utc.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve case-insensitive `strptime` literals."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"e7038b722b4ae03e235594943a0a4cfa054b3ba2","body":"**Use Python's week-date separator disambiguation.**\n\nAt `src/policy/crq/utc.ts:167`, `parseUtc('2026-W01-12:00:00')` selects `2026-W01-1` as the date. It consumes `2` as the separator, then rejects `:00:00`. Python selects the hyphen after `W01` and accepts the timestamp. Replace the longest-prefix rule with Python's disambiguation rule. ([raw.githubusercontent.com](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.14.10/Modules/_datetimemodule.c))\n\nBased on learnings, defer this minor compatibility fix to a follow-up issue.","id":"5f1c390b316da6e1aa09708570785f9385041124192c2db19e18c5090ddaa9d5","intervals":[[167,167]],"path":"src/policy/crq/utc.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use Python's week-date separator disambiguation."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"4f63bd7f645d76bf085363cb35562699a4f6c4c8","body":"**Validate all paths before updating receipt aggregates.**\n\nIn `src/policy/crq/statusSummary.ts`, a matching completed receipt with `paths: [{\"disposition\":\"deleted\"}, null]` passes the identity checks. Line 469 increments `proven_terminal` before path validation fails. Line 484 then also increments `unverified`. The target and earlier exclusions also remain recorded.\n\nValidate the complete receipt into local values first. Update counts, targets and exclusions only after validation succeeds.","id":"b76e67153163aaf533097fe2efa56bfd9f364d072cf79f6d556332f2fe4cc1e0","intervals":[[469,469]],"path":"src/policy/crq/statusSummary.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Validate all paths before updating receipt aggregates."}],"head":"5464d71ca4e1cef04ba662a8db4dd93eb06cb71c","head_tree":"fd9b086373c60203765fe780f899178a146a7825","input_scope":[{"blob":"6207a1b5ffc3cd99cffdaef7a56ad3fa9d664218","intervals":[[1,673]],"path":"src/policy/crq/coverageUtilization.ts"},{"blob":"c70f1d1d782d1cdc35da51087d59ac3b3faf5877","intervals":[[1,645]],"path":"src/policy/crq/jsonValue.ts"},{"blob":"3f346a83e97dd56380787eeb4f2d2556c8ed1d5e","intervals":[[1,155]],"path":"src/policy/crq/receiptIdentity.ts"},{"blob":"1dc3b625e63e4297f4cb76453f80dde1243b6f92","intervals":[[1,487]],"path":"src/policy/crq/repairBinding.ts"},{"blob":"eac620f5c26a15e8803190eee7b72b451bb2a2d3","intervals":[[1,422]],"path":"src/policy/crq/repairGates.ts"},{"blob":"c99b996944fd339cb55c658326bfb67d41a571ee","intervals":[[1,308]],"path":"src/policy/crq/state.ts"},{"blob":"4f63bd7f645d76bf085363cb35562699a4f6c4c8","intervals":[[1,972]],"path":"src/policy/crq/statusSummary.ts"},{"blob":"e7038b722b4ae03e235594943a0a4cfa054b3ba2","intervals":[[1,390]],"path":"src/policy/crq/utc.ts"}],"job_id":"f8ad084d4746ab5235f9958d439cd2fda3c9e8dccb759b87